    Ruling 17 (orchestrator 10:20): sentence-lock text adjudication by the independent second recogniser; G18 compares the final with an adjudicated lock
    
    When a pinned run's own decode differs from the pin's approved text in a locked span: a number, name or negation
    difference always holds (L-v 2; any digit or an ordinal counts as a number); otherwise scribe_v1 on the acquired window
    decides: it must read the approved words AT every difference (they and a neighbour on each side aligned and
    consecutive) for the lock to take them (digest recomputed, three readings recorded); the run's reading, or neither,
    holds naming the three readings. G18's identity reference for an adjudicated lock is the lock text; unadjudicated
    locks unchanged. pipeline/second_recogniser.py is the audited file of branch ruling7, verbatim.
    Tests (test_ruling17_lock, 12): agree / run-side / neither / negation 2-1 / number / name / no difference; the audit's
    cases (the approved word elsewhere in the span; a deletion read as another word; ordinals and grouped numbers); the
    real Nov 12 clip_01 head (scribe_v1 'I think' vs the pin's 'I mean,') holds; G18 against an adjudicated lock. The
    Nov 10 G18 fixtures still fail (test_word_diff TestYesterdaysFinal, GPU0).
    Audit batch33 cycle 1 on Heimdall: deepseek FAIL (F1, F2, F3), qwen27b PASS; consensus F2 (deletion read as another
    word) and F3 (numbers) implemented, F1 (not agreed) implemented anyway as the stricter positional reading.
    
